From 331af7b2a1f7e287d15a411b710f73ddbaa02a57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 21:02:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] html: honour text color alpha (transparent -> invisible text,
 rgba -> ExtGState)

The bridge built text fill colors from the RGB channels only, so
`color: transparent` rendered opaque black and `rgba(..., a)` rendered
fully opaque. OCR text layers (transparent spans over a page scan) came
out as black text on top of the image.

Text runs with a < 255 now render in their own q/Q scope: a == 0 uses
text rendering mode 3 (invisible but selectable/extractable), 0 < a < 255
loads a fill-alpha ExtGState. Opaque runs are unchanged. The glyph-run
inline background pass gets the same ExtGState treatment.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
